{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And the children of Israel shall come.</b> It was the seventh night of Passover. And there is a difficulty, for at the end of parashat Shelach they explained the eight threads of tzitzit as corresponding to the eight days that Israel tarried from when they left Egypt until they said song at the sea — implying that on the eighth day they said song. And one may answer that further on it counts from when they prepared themselves to leave, from the eve of Passover when they slaughtered the Paschal offering: they knew they would leave the next day and were preparing provisions for the journey. Even so, they did not prepare everything needed, as it is said: וגם צדה לא עשו להם — 'and they did not prepare provisions for themselves.'"], :book :exodus, :voice :daat-zkenim, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:03:06.436743567Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}